#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# slice_density_plot3d

#% text
# `slice_density_plot3d(f, surface, [x, a, b], [y, c, d], [z, e, f])` draws the values of a function as colours on surfaces in a box.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Surfaces: `"CenterPlanes"` (default), `"BackPlanes"`, `"XStackedPlanes"`, `"YStackedPlanes"`, `"ZStackedPlanes"`, `"DiagonalPlanes"`, `"CenterSphere"`, an equation, a region (`sphere`, `cylinder`, `infinite_plane`, `half_plane`, `implicit_region`) or a list of them.

#% item
# `element([x, y, z], region)` instead of the ranges takes the region's bounds.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
slice_density_plot3d(exp(-(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)), "CenterPlanes", [x, -2, 2], [y, -2, 2], [z, -2, 2])
#% output
#= image("slice_density_plot3d.files/slice_density_plot3d-1.svgz")

#% cell
slice_density_plot3d(x * y * z, x^2 + y^2 - z == 0, [x, -1, 1], [y, -1, 1], [z, -1, 1])
#% output
#= image("slice_density_plot3d.files/slice_density_plot3d-2.svgz")

